# Alembic Database Migrations

This directory contains database migration scripts and configuration managed via [Alembic](https://alembic.sqlalchemy.org/) with async PostgreSQL (`asyncpg`) support.

---

## Directory Structure

```
backend/alembic/
├── README              # This documentation
├── env.py              # Alembic environment configuration (async DB runner & metadata bindings)
├── script.py.mako      # Template for newly generated migration revisions
└── versions/           # Migration revision scripts
    └── 1208df9f664f_initial_tables_prompts_tags_settings.py
```

---

## Schema Overview

The initial migration (`1208df9f664f`) provisions the following core tables:

| Table | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `global_prompts` | System-level master prompts, tracking draft text, versions, and edit status. |
| `scoring_prompts` | Evaluation and scoring prompt templates with draft and version tracking. |
| `prompt_snapshots` | Point-in-time published snapshots of prompts (including interest prompts in `JSONB`). |
| `rating_tags` | Taxonomy tags with associated weights and active flags for scoring/tagging. |
| `app_settings` | Key-value application settings using PostgreSQL `JSONB` for arbitrary configuration values. |

---

## Common Commands

Run these commands from the `backend/` directory:

### Apply Migrations
Upgrade to the latest schema version:
```bash
alembic upgrade head
```

### Rollback Migrations
Revert the last applied migration:
```bash
alembic downgrade -1
```

### Generate a New Migration
Generate an autodetected migration based on model changes in `app.db.models`:
```bash
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe_changes_here"
```

Create an empty migration script:
```bash
alembic revision -m "describe_changes_here"
```

### Check Migration Status
View the current revision applied to the database:
```bash
alembic current
```

View migration history:
```bash
alembic history --verbose
```